{"text": "AUTHORIZATION FOR MEDICATION ADMINISTRATION AT SCHOOL\nSchool year 2025-26 · Fernhill Elementary School · Health Office fax (530) 555-0193\nRequired by Education Code § 49423. A new form is needed each school year and whenever a dose changes.\nStudent\nStudent: ESPINOZA-KAUR, Mateo (\"Teo\") · Date of birth: 09/22/2016 · Grade 4 · Room 12 · Teacher: Ms. Bellamy\nHome address: 3317 Covey Run Court, Chico, CA 95973\nHealth plan: Bluestem Health Plan, member ID BHP-4471-20936-02, group 70318\nDiagnoses and medications ordered\nMedication\tDose\tRoute\tWhen\nalbuterol HFA 90 mcg\t2 puffs with spacer\tInhaled\t15 min before PE and recess; every 4 hrs as needed for wheeze\nmethylphenidate ER 18 mg\t1 tablet\tOral\t12:15 after Lunch\nepinephrine auto-injector 0.15 mg\t1 injection\tIM\tAt first sign of anaphylaxis, then Call 911\n\nDiagnoses: moderate persistent asthma (ICD-10 J45.40); ADHD, combined presentation; peanut and tree-nut allergy with anaphylaxis in March 2024. No known drug allergies.\nSelf-carry: the student may carry and self-administer the inhaler. He may NOT carry the methylphenidate (Schedule II); it stays locked in the Health Office.\nStorage and supply: the pharmacy label must match this order. Current fills are from Kestrel Pharmacy, East Avenue store: Rx 7730418 (methylphenidate, filled 8/11/25) and Rx 7730422 (EpiPen Jr two-pack, expires 04/2026).\nPrescriber\nAnjali Iyer, MD · Thistledown Pediatric Group · 1850 Bidwell Parkway, Suite 210, Chico, CA 95926\nOffice 530-555-0148 · after hours 530-555-0149 · NPI 1568204937 · DEA FI4482093 · CA Lic. A 118562\nPrescriber signature: /s/ A. Iyer · Date: August 8, 2025\nParent/guardian\nI ask that school staff give the medication above to my child as ordered and I allow the school nurse to talk with the prescriber and the pharmacy about it.\nMother: Gurpreet Kaur · cell 530.555.0162 · gkaur.rn@mailhaven.example · works nights at Ridgeview, so text first\nFather: Rafael Espinoza · cell (530) 555-0177 · work 530-555-0105 ext. 31 · rafa.espinoza@quarrycreekfire.example\nThe parents are separated; Teo is with his father on alternating weeks. Either parent may pick up medication. Sister Anaya (Grade 1, Room 5) has no medications at school.\nSignature: G. Kaur · Date: 8/12/2025\nHealth Office use\nReceived and reviewed by Tamika Hinds, RN, District Nurse (RN Lic. 95088214) on Aug. 14, 2025. Section 504 plan updated the same day. Counted 20 tablets in; next Refill due about Sept. 9.\nEmergency plan: Give epinephrine first. Do not give Benadryl instead. Call 911, then Mrs. Kaur, then Mr. Espinoza. For a Field Trip, Corinne Bellamy carries the red bag and has been trained (9/3/25). Questions: thinds@qcusd.example or District Health Services, 530-555-0100.\n\nQuarry Creek Unified School District · Form HS-12 (rev. 2025-26) · Student ID 60044817 · CONFIDENTIAL HEALTH RECORD", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "444 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Mateo (", " Bellamy", "Anjali Iyer", "Gurpreet Kaur", "Rafael Espinoza", "Tamika Hinds", "Corinne Bellamy"], "companies": ["Bluestem Health Plan", "Kestrel Pharmacy", "Thistledown Pediatric Group", "Ridgeview", "Quarry Creek Unified School District"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 1.5999999977648258, "modelMs": 26132.89999999851, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 60, "text": "AUTHORIZATION FOR MEDICATION ADMINISTRATION AT SCHOOL\nSchool", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "AUTHORIZATION FOR MEDICATION ADMINISTRATION AT SCHOOL School"}, {"start": 76, "end": 102, "text": "Fernhill Elementary School", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Fernhill Elementary School"}, {"start": 123, "end": 137, "te